{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197976-help-me-classify-and-stat-up-umbrood","id":1197976,"title":"Help Me Classify and Stat Up Umbrood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-21T08:17:36-07:00","id":1197976,"title":"Help Me Classify and Stat Up Umbrood","content":"So, as a new ST, I'm trying to adjudicate a game that pulls heavily from a mix of Aztec mythology, Mexican folk religion, Catholicism and 30's UFO lore. Having little experience running the game, I can't help but fear that I'm in a little over my head trying to incorporate all the weird Bygones and Spirits that would represent such a wide range of sources. Anybody have any suggestions on where to start?<br /> <br /> For a specific example of what I need help with, where in the Umbrood hierarchies would the Tzitzimitl be? How would they be stated? What charms would they have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T02:43:13-07:00","id":1198279,"title":"","content":"When it comes to umbrood hierarchies, it's fairly arbitrary. In the books it's heavily implied that categorisations of umbrood into their various ranks is something that Etherites came up with, and only really holds any consistency for them. The Umbrood themselves may only play into it just to mock them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the terms Werewolf use are pretty simple.<br /> Celestine: Literal spirit embodiments of the physical world. They are the gods, and their disappearance is the literal end of their aspect's being. Luna and Gaia being the prime examples<br /> Incarna: The most powerful spirits you or anyone is likely to encounter. They are effectively aspects of their respective celestine. If you wanted to talk to Luna, you'd probably be talking to one of her incarna instead. they can be destroyed, but easily replaced when need be.<br /> Jagling: The commanders on the ground. These guys are more powerful spirits than the Gafflings, and will generally be the ones leading assults or carrying out duties. They report to their respective incarna, and hold a level of sentience. You will probably encounter these guys if you gain a broods attention, or if you happen to be powerful enough to summon them. Jagglings can be &quot;promoted&quot; to incarna as the need arises.<br /> Gaffling: Mooks, They do the grunt work, have varying degrees of sentience. These are the spirits you are most likely to encounter just shouting out into the umbra.<br /> Engling: Literally born to die and be happy about doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just for completness sake, the way Etherites class umbrood is as follows:<br /> <br /> At the very top are the Lords, which probably take the role similar to Celestine, after that things get a little messy.<br /> <br /> They divide them into two &quot;branches&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;On the one branch, called the Right Branch, are more or less permanent positions, according great respect, but proportionally lesser power.&quot;<br /> <br /> It looks like this:<br /> High cardinals<br /> Low Cardinals<br /> Bishops<br /> Monsignots<br /> <br /> &quot;In the other branch of the tree, called the Left Branch, - These are elected positions and the spirits imbued with these ranks can have them removed at any time by a majority vote.&quot;<br /> <br /> Chief Executor<br /> Upper Managers<br /> Lower Managers<br /> Technicians<br /> <br /> Then there's the Accountants, which are basically civil servants? They do all the grindwork behind the scenes and answer to.... eh?<br /> <br /> How well these ranks fit into the Werewolf model is variable at best. But as I said earlier, it's not all that necessary to use this system. Stick with the werewolf one and only delve into the Etherite complications if it helps.<br /> <br /> Focus instead should be on the hierarchy in the lore of it all. I don't know much bout either Aztec of Mexican lore, but I can't imagine it's too difficult to look at the hierarchies of the gods and just take it wholesale.<br /> When it comes to stating them up, all you need to do is judge based on what you think is appropriate to what the gods are known for.<br /> The four stats you need are:<br /> Rage - The Fight stat<br /> Gnosis- The Thinking stat<br /> Willpower- The everything else stat<br /> Essence/Power - How much quintessence they hold, and how they power their charms.<br /> <br /> Rage, Gnosis and WP tend to be a scale from 1 to 10.<br /> Essence tends to be in multiples of 10, and can go as high at a couple hundred depending on how powerful they are.<br /> <br /> As for charms, you can just make them up based on what these gods are known for. If you want somewhere to start, then this is a really good list of a bunch of charms used by spirits in werewolf<br /> <a href=\"http://dusk.wikia.com/wiki/Spirit_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">http://dusk.wikia.com/wiki/Spirit_Charms</a><br /> <br /> This should give you a starting point, but don't feel restricted by it at all.<br /> <br /> Book of Worlds has a few stated up Angel characters which might help too. Other than that I can only recommend checking out the Axis Mundi for more spirit ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 03-23-2018, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}